        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Residual wood, softwood, under bark, air dried, u=20%, at forest road</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Residual wood, softwood, under bark, air dried, u=20%, at forest road
The  volume refers to the wood not including the bark.;
Synonyms: Fichte, Spruce; 
UUID: 203bc266-3227-30bc-b938-24f2bfd589b7
Natural drying in the forest. Land use of forest is already considered with the "softwood, standing, in forest" process. Thus it is not again included here. Air emissions released from the wood are not accounted for because the same emissions would occur if the wood would not be used.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Naturaly dried on staples for 2 years. Shrinkeage for spruce
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: see Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: The assumption that the volume change of spruce is the same as for other softwood is considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_203bc266-3227-30bc-b938-24f2bfd589b7.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
